WEBVTT

00:02.378 --> 00:05.644
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.749 --> 00:08.947
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.053 --> 00:12.650
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.759 --> 00:15.661
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.763 --> 00:18.961
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.067 --> 00:22.367
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.471 --> 00:23.939
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.041 --> 00:25.668
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.777 --> 00:30.613
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.623 --> 00:38.388
- Mom, where's Dad?
- Over across the street.

00:38.493 --> 00:40.758
He's collecting Cleveland's mail
while he's out of town.

00:40.863 --> 00:42.263
Black guy mail!

00:42.366 --> 00:44.732
Peter, you're just supposed to
pick up Cleveland's mail,

00:44.835 --> 00:45.894
not go through it.

00:46.004 --> 00:48.269
Lois, black people are
different than you and I.

00:48.374 --> 00:50.342
And me, I find that hilarious.

00:50.444 --> 00:52.969
Boy, Cleveland gets a lot of magazines.

00:53.080 --> 00:56.745
<i>Grape Soda Today,
Orange Soda Quarterly,</i>

00:56.852 --> 00:58.319
<i>The Fruit Punch Reader.</i>

00:58.420 --> 00:59.649
Hey, what you got there, Stewie?

00:59.789 --> 01:01.222
<i>Ooh! Mustache Aficionado.</i>

01:03.559 --> 01:06.928
Wow, look at these men!
What class. What grace.

01:07.031 --> 01:09.397
And all because of a little upper-lip hair.

01:09.500 --> 01:12.026
Lois, I am gonna grow a mustache.

01:12.137 --> 01:14.698
Then I'll have it made,
like the Monopoly guy.

01:14.807 --> 01:16.867
Except when he goes directly to jail.

01:16.977 --> 01:19.538
<i>I wish I could tell you that
the Monopoly guy</i>

01:19.647 --> 01:22.776
<i>fought the good fight,
and the sisters let him be.</i>

01:22.885 --> 01:27.620
<i>I wish I could tell you that,
but prison is no fairytale world.</i>

01:32.398 --> 01:36.165
Hey, Rupert, what if the refrigerator
was a monster that talked like this?

01:36.270 --> 01:39.901
I am a monster.
I am going to bite your fingers.

01:40.009 --> 01:42.843
Here I come. I'm going to get you.

01:42.946 --> 01:44.743
Ah! I don't want to play anymore.
Normal voice, normal voice.

01:44.848 --> 01:46.749
The refrigerator can't hurt me. Okay?

01:47.719 --> 01:49.950
Oh, my God, Dad! What's on your face?

01:50.055 --> 01:51.853
Meg, it goes by many names.

01:51.958 --> 01:56.293
Soup Strainer, Lip Whiskers,
and, until recently, Giant Horse Vagina,

01:56.398 --> 01:57.956
but I prefer the term mustache.

01:58.300 --> 02:00.132
Oh! I think it's sexy.

02:00.236 --> 02:02.467
- I think it's gay.
- It's not gay, Brian.

02:02.573 --> 02:04.804
If I'm gay, then Freddie Mercury was gay.

02:04.910 --> 02:06.775
Freddie Mercury,
the lead singer of Queen?

02:06.878 --> 02:07.971
He was incredibly gay.

02:08.080 --> 02:11.642
He was not. He had a mustache,
which is practically like a wedding ring.

02:11.752 --> 02:14.085
I imagine you're gonna be
much more of a stern father

02:14.188 --> 02:15.622
now that you have a mustache.

02:15.724 --> 02:18.249
Well, Chris, there may be more
lap sitting than there's been,

02:18.361 --> 02:20.761
and I might answer
most of your questions with a story,

02:20.864 --> 02:22.730
but mostly, my mustache tells people

02:22.833 --> 02:25.632
that there is a 90% chance
that I am poorly educated,

02:25.737 --> 02:28.639
that I keep upscale porn magazines
out in the open,

02:28.741 --> 02:31.472
and that I listen to the Little River Band
with giant headphones.

02:31.579 --> 02:35.745
Ew! That's the ugliest thing
the fat man's grown since that horse leg.

02:35.851 --> 02:37.683
Hey, Peter, have you seen my... Ah!

02:37.788 --> 02:39.983
Brian, I'm sorry,
but what do I keep saying?

02:40.090 --> 02:43.721
Do not stand behind me.
Because I will get scared.

02:47.500 --> 02:49.833
<i>And now back to
One Tree Hill.</i>

02:49.937 --> 02:51.872
<i>Dude, let me tell you something.</i>

02:51.974 --> 02:55.035
<i>There is nothing that'll ever happen
in the rest of our lives</i>

02:55.144 --> 02:57.978
<i>that's as important as
what's going on right here,</i>

02:58.082 --> 03:00.950
<i>right now, in high school,
by these lockers.</i>

03:01.052 --> 03:02.918
<i>I've got so many problems.</i>

03:03.022 --> 03:06.686
<i>Hey. Nothing that can't be fixed
by staring at a lake.</i>

03:06.793 --> 03:11.232
<i>High school is such a serious thing</i>

03:11.333 --> 03:15.464
<i>These problems matter</i>

03:15.739 --> 03:17.901
God, these high school students
are lame.

03:18.009 --> 03:20.240
I'm a freakin' baby,
and I'm cooler than they are.

03:20.345 --> 03:21.813
What the hell do you know
about high school?

03:21.914 --> 03:25.043
Are you kidding? These kids today
are so easy to manipulate.

03:25.152 --> 03:27.178
If you plopped me
in the middle of a high school,

03:27.288 --> 03:29.313
I could be the most popular kid
there in a week.

03:29.424 --> 03:32.258
Really?
Would you care to place a wager on that?

03:32.361 --> 03:33.693
Absolutely. What are the stakes?

03:33.797 --> 03:35.789
Okay, if I win, and you can't do it,

03:35.900 --> 03:39.564
you have to put your nose in Meg's hat
and take an eight-second inhale.

03:39.672 --> 03:42.073
Okay, and if I win, you have to go online

03:42.175 --> 03:45.543
<i>and download that footage of
the dancing baby from Ally McBeal,</i>

03:45.646 --> 03:48.411
and you have to forward it
to all your friends with the message,

03:48.517 --> 03:51.146
"Oh, my God,
look what I just found online!

03:51.254 --> 03:53.280
"Isn't this the funniest thing
you've ever seen?"

03:53.390 --> 03:54.358
- So, is it a bet?
- Yeah, fine.

03:54.459 --> 03:55.448
- Kiss on it? Oh!
- What?

04:01.835 --> 04:03.565
Wow, Dad, you're up early.

04:03.671 --> 04:06.197
Yep, it's
a mustache kind of morning, Chris.

04:06.308 --> 04:10.040
I watched the sun rise in my jeans,
jean shirt and jean jacket.

04:10.146 --> 04:12.741
Gosh, mustache culture is pretty cool.

04:12.850 --> 04:16.150
You betcha, son. I'm gonna make you
some hash browns for breakfast,

04:16.254 --> 04:19.555
and then later I'm gonna take you down
to the whorehouse to lose your virginity.

04:19.660 --> 04:21.150
- Would you like that?
- Would I?

04:21.261 --> 04:23.230
Wow, that's a way better present
than that buff hamster

04:23.331 --> 04:24.629
you got me last Christmas.

04:28.283 --> 04:30.878
Dad, all it's done is run on that wheel
for the past three weeks.

04:30.987 --> 04:32.888
Yeah, looks like it's in pretty good shape.

04:32.990 --> 04:34.753
- Can I pick it up?
- I wouldn't.

04:37.974 --> 04:39.772
Boy, you know,
I've always wanted to come in here,

04:39.877 --> 04:42.403
and now that I got a mustache,
the timing feels right.

04:42.514 --> 04:44.210
Wow, all this stuff looks pretty good.

04:44.317 --> 04:47.412
- Can we get some salami and...
- Brian, Brian, let me handle this.

04:50.392 --> 04:52.520
- Peter, what are you doing?
- Speaking Italian.

04:55.165 --> 04:57.794
Peter, you can't speak Italian
just because you have a mustache.

05:14.758 --> 05:17.626
Hi there.
Is this the Quahog Mustache Society?

05:17.729 --> 05:20.665
Yes, it is. What's the secret password?

05:20.766 --> 05:22.598
- Mustache.
- All right. Come on in.

05:24.905 --> 05:28.138
Good afternoon, mustache wearers.
Don't forget to help yourself to the buffet.

05:28.243 --> 05:31.179
There's spaghetti and meatballs,
powdered donuts and bubblegum.

05:31.281 --> 05:33.750
- Point of mustache.
- The chair recognizes your mustache.

05:33.884 --> 05:36.251
Have we discussed what to send
Wilford Brimley next month,

05:36.354 --> 05:38.755
as it is the 70th birthday of his mustache?

05:38.858 --> 05:41.794
Oh, I think we just send a nice card.
Just make sure it has a mustache on it.

05:41.895 --> 05:44.194
- Point of mustache.
- The chair recognizes your mustache.

05:44.299 --> 05:47.201
What can we, as citizens,
do about mustache awareness?

05:47.303 --> 05:48.361
Good mustache question.

05:48.471 --> 05:50.440
We have a new product
in our mustache catalog

05:50.540 --> 05:53.840
that makes a great stocking stuffer.
We call it the Must-Stash.

05:53.945 --> 05:56.073
The slogan is, " You must stash
your Must-Stash in the mustache."

05:56.181 --> 05:57.512
That'll be all for today.

05:57.616 --> 05:58.777
- Good mustache.
- Good mustache.

06:08.165 --> 06:11.363
All right, dog, here we go.
Prepare to lose a bet,

06:11.469 --> 06:14.406
'cause I'm about to become
the most popular boy in school.

06:15.509 --> 06:18.001
Excuse me, pardon me,
are you the cool children?

06:18.112 --> 06:21.048
- Yeah. Who are you?
- My name is Zac Sawyer.

06:21.150 --> 06:24.450
I just transferred here from
Rich Expensive Car-Driving

06:24.554 --> 06:26.147
Sex-Having High School.

06:26.257 --> 06:30.456
- Whoa! That sounds awesome.
- No, it's lame. Everything's lame.

06:30.562 --> 06:33.556
Wow, if he says one more cool thing,
he's in.

06:33.667 --> 06:37.695
I wear long sleeve shirts under short
sleeve shirts under long sleeve shirts.

06:37.839 --> 06:38.863
- Wow!
- Oh, my God!

06:38.973 --> 06:40.566
- Oh, my God, you're so cool!
- You're so awesome!

06:40.676 --> 06:42.668
You've checkmated my teenage cynicism!

06:42.779 --> 06:47.217
Excellent. I'm a bigger hit with the kids
than Will Smith and his nice clean rap.

06:48.086 --> 06:49.246
<i>Whoo!</i>

06:49.354 --> 06:50.344
<i>Ha! Ha!</i>

06:50.457 --> 06:52.322
<i>I respect women
when I'm on a date</i>

06:52.725 --> 06:55.126
<i>I take them to the park
or maybe a museum</i>

06:55.229 --> 06:57.255
<i>And I only try to kiss them
if they're ready</i>

06:57.365 --> 06:58.333
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

06:58.434 --> 07:00.334
<i>What, what, what, what
I say what, what</i>

07:00.436 --> 07:02.803
<i>Help out your mom and dad
by getting a job</i>

07:02.906 --> 07:04.704
<i>So you can help pay for school supplies</i>

07:04.809 --> 07:05.867
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

07:05.977 --> 07:07.878
<i>Say ho!</i>

07:07.980 --> 07:10.643
<i>Wipe your shoes on the mat
when you come in the house</i>

07:10.750 --> 07:12.446
<i>Someone just cleaned that floor</i>

07:12.553 --> 07:13.520
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

07:13.621 --> 07:14.610
<i>Say what, what!</i>

07:14.723 --> 07:16.088
<i>Ha! Ha!</i>

07:18.962 --> 07:21.090
Peter, don't you think
you're kind of letting that mustache

07:21.198 --> 07:22.460
consume your personality?

07:22.566 --> 07:23.556
Shut up, Brian.

07:23.668 --> 07:25.967
I am part
of a very special community now.

07:26.072 --> 07:28.541
People with mustaches
look out for each other.

07:28.642 --> 07:30.701
Hey. Oh, hey!

07:32.280 --> 07:34.010
<i>- Hey!
- Hey. Jeffrey,</i>

07:34.116 --> 07:35.743
<i>- Peter Griffin has a mustache!
- No way!</i>

07:35.851 --> 07:37.410
<i>- Way!
- Ohhh!</i>

07:37.521 --> 07:38.545
I know!

07:40.565 --> 07:43.660
Oh, my God, Peter, look!
McBurgertown is on fire!

07:46.139 --> 07:49.109
It's out of control!
We need someone to man the other hose!

07:49.210 --> 07:51.805
Hey, that guy has a mustache! Grab him!

07:52.081 --> 07:55.415
We need your help! Take this hose!

07:55.519 --> 07:59.287
Uh... Okay, you just want me to spray
the water at the fire and try to put it out?

07:59.391 --> 08:01.256
He knows everything about what we do.

08:01.360 --> 08:03.295
Of course he does.
Look at that giant horse vagina.

08:06.166 --> 08:07.395
Help!

08:07.502 --> 08:10.836
Oh, my God!
There's somebody trapped inside!

08:10.940 --> 08:13.569
Wait. If I go in there, I could get hurt.

08:13.677 --> 08:17.843
No. No, with great mustache
comes great responsibility.

08:24.525 --> 08:25.890
My mustache!

08:29.065 --> 08:30.965
No!

08:31.067 --> 08:34.060
God bless you, sir, you saved my life.

08:34.171 --> 08:35.935
But at what cost? At what cost?

08:40.441 --> 08:44.708
- Peter, have you seen Brian?
- No, Lois, I have not.

08:44.813 --> 08:47.578
Well, I haven't seen him
since this morning, and I...

08:47.684 --> 08:49.084
What is that on your head?

08:49.186 --> 08:52.350
It's a mustache, Lois!
What, you never seen a mustache before?

08:52.457 --> 08:54.358
Lois, would you mind
calling the police or something?

08:54.460 --> 08:55.427
Quiet, mustache!

08:55.528 --> 08:58.657
Oh, my God! Peter, I know you're upset
about losing that thing,

08:58.766 --> 09:01.395
but get a grip on yourself.
Let Brian down.

09:01.503 --> 09:04.405
No. I'm not living my life
without a mustache.

09:04.508 --> 09:07.068
Even if sometimes
my mustache has Alpo gas.

09:08.246 --> 09:09.235
Mustache fart.

09:11.383 --> 09:13.352
Hello, I'm looking for Peter Griffin.

09:13.453 --> 09:16.321
- I'm Peter Griffin.
- Mr. Griffin, my name is Todd Meyers.

09:16.424 --> 09:18.518
I'm the man
you rescued from McBurgertown.

09:18.627 --> 09:21.563
Oh, yeah, you're the guy
who cost me my mustache.

09:21.664 --> 09:23.461
What, did you come over here
to rape my daughter?

09:23.566 --> 09:26.799
No, I own the restaurant.
And to show my gratitude,

09:26.905 --> 09:31.206
I'd like to offer you a lifetime supply
of McBurgertown burgers.

09:31.944 --> 09:33.173
Free burgers?

09:33.280 --> 09:37.149
Oh, man, this is a way better offer
than the one I got from Helen Hunt.

09:37.251 --> 09:40.689
- You wanna have sex?
- No.

09:40.790 --> 09:43.760
No, no, no, no, no.

09:43.861 --> 09:46.422
No. No.

09:50.870 --> 09:53.897
Peter, you should really slow down.
You've already had, like, 30 hamburgers.

09:54.009 --> 09:57.776
Shut up, Brian.
It relieves the pain of mustachelessness.

09:57.880 --> 10:00.748
And it's working. I no longer feel the pain.

10:00.851 --> 10:03.013
Come to think of it,
I can't really feel anything

10:03.121 --> 10:04.486
on the left half of my body.

10:04.589 --> 10:07.081
Really? That doesn't sound good.

10:07.192 --> 10:09.388
Peter, are you winking at me?

10:11.665 --> 10:13.691
Oh, my God, someone call an ambulance!

10:16.839 --> 10:19.673
Doctor, what happened?
Is he gonna be okay?

10:19.777 --> 10:22.269
Mrs. Griffin,
your husband has had a stroke.

10:22.380 --> 10:25.179
The left half of his body
is completely paralyzed.

10:25.317 --> 10:26.716
Oh, my God!

10:26.819 --> 10:28.549
Peter, sweetheart, how do you feel?

10:28.655 --> 10:29.645
Uh...

10:29.757 --> 10:32.921
Had better days, Lois. Had better days.

10:37.935 --> 10:41.736
Mom, it's been three months.
When is Dad gonna get better?

10:41.840 --> 10:43.934
Chris, I've already explained this to you.

10:44.043 --> 10:47.207
Your father had a stroke, and
it may take him a long time to recover.

10:47.314 --> 10:50.478
Lois!
Bring me another beer, please!

10:55.926 --> 10:56.893
Uh...

10:56.993 --> 11:00.362
Lois. You mind telling me
what the hell you think you're doing?

11:00.466 --> 11:04.665
- I'm handing you a beer.
- You are handing it to my stroke arm.

11:04.771 --> 11:07.764
This is my good arm.
Bring the beer over here!

11:08.410 --> 11:09.900
That's better!

11:14.785 --> 11:17.380
So, I'm shaving last night
at this make-out party.

11:17.489 --> 11:20.357
I took a bunch of pictures.
You can see them on my MySpace page,

11:20.459 --> 11:24.055
along with my favorite songs and movies,
and things that other people have created,

11:24.164 --> 11:26.395
but that I use to express my individualism.

11:26.501 --> 11:28.299
I have a MySpace page, too.

11:28.403 --> 11:30.099
Yeah, I have mine ironically.

11:30.206 --> 11:33.005
Hey, why don't you guys get lost?
I have to talk to Connie.

11:35.246 --> 11:36.737
- Hey, guess what?
- What?

11:36.848 --> 11:38.316
That's what. No, but seriously,

11:38.417 --> 11:39.748
there's something I want to
talk to you about.

11:39.852 --> 11:41.946
Sure, Zac. Anything for you.

11:42.055 --> 11:43.956
You wanna go out to Anal Point
this weekend,

11:44.058 --> 11:45.320
see what all the buzz is about?

11:45.426 --> 11:48.521
OMG, that'd be so awesome!

11:48.631 --> 11:51.294
Sweet.
We're gonna have a real raging time.

11:51.401 --> 11:54.098
Before you know it,
we'll be like an old married couple.

12:19.574 --> 12:21.371
- Uh, Lois?
- Yeah?

12:21.475 --> 12:23.876
Uh, Peter's getting in the car.

12:33.192 --> 12:36.026
<i>Uh oh, overflow, population
common group, but it'll do</i>

12:36.129 --> 12:37.187
<i>Save yourself, serve yourself</i>

12:37.297 --> 12:39.528
<i>World serves its own needs
Listen to your heart bleed</i>

12:39.634 --> 12:42.195
<i>Tell me with the rapture
and the reverent in the right, right</i>

12:42.304 --> 12:44.239
<i>You vitriolic, patriotic, slam, fight</i>

12:44.341 --> 12:46.502
<i>Bright light, feeling pretty psyched</i>

12:46.610 --> 12:50.343
<i>It's the end of the world as we know it</i>

12:56.056 --> 12:59.049
Stroke! Stroke! Stroke!

12:59.160 --> 13:00.719
Stop mocking me!

13:05.869 --> 13:07.462
Well, Brian, you've lost your bet.

13:07.572 --> 13:10.337
I, or rather, my alter ego, Zac Sawyer,

13:10.442 --> 13:13.412
am currently the most popular boy
at James Woods High.

13:13.513 --> 13:15.744
Well, Stewie,
you got the best of me on this one.

13:15.850 --> 13:18.820
Congratulations.
I guess you'll be hanging up your wig now.

13:18.920 --> 13:21.446
Oh, no, Brian.
I'm enjoying myself too much.

13:21.557 --> 13:24.254
Do you know that I've got a date
with Connie D'Amico

13:24.361 --> 13:26.193
this Saturday night at Anal Point?

13:26.298 --> 13:27.959
Ah! I've heard about that place.

13:28.067 --> 13:30.160
Really? What's it like?
'Cause I have no idea.

13:30.269 --> 13:35.299
Well, I suppose if you imagine it
like a parking space that you think,

13:35.410 --> 13:38.005
"Gosh, there's no way
I'm gonna be able to fit in there,"

13:38.113 --> 13:41.572
but then you fold in the side-view mirrors
and sure enough, "Well, look at that."

13:41.685 --> 13:43.176
Well, in that scenario, it sounds like

13:43.287 --> 13:45.153
I'd rather be the
parking space than the car.

13:45.257 --> 13:46.690
Yeah, that's what I've always guessed.

13:50.597 --> 13:53.192
I hate being all strokey.

13:53.535 --> 13:56.266
This is all your fault, McBurgertown.

13:56.372 --> 14:01.277
You and your delicious hamburgers.
I swear, I'll get back at you someday

14:01.379 --> 14:04.440
for what you did to me
and what you did to Wimpy!

14:04.550 --> 14:09.922
I would gladly pay you Tuesday
for a hamburger today.

14:10.024 --> 14:14.428
If only there was some way
I could be like everybody else again.

14:29.617 --> 14:31.916
- How long was I in there?
- About five minutes.

14:32.020 --> 14:34.387
Why are we not funding this?

14:37.261 --> 14:40.754
Sweetheart, that's incredible!
And it only took five minutes?

14:40.866 --> 14:42.767
Five minutes.
I went in there, they injected me

14:42.869 --> 14:46.431
with a little bit of that fetal crap, and bam!
Good old gambling man Peter.

14:46.540 --> 14:49.032
And now I can take my revenge
on McBurgertown!

14:49.144 --> 14:51.909
- Wait. What?
- It's their fault I had a stroke, Brian.

14:52.014 --> 14:53.243
And I'm gonna sue them for it.

14:53.350 --> 14:55.945
Peter, you ate 30 hamburgers.
It was your own fault.

14:56.053 --> 14:59.683
Yeah, besides, Peter, those companies
have huge legal divisions.

14:59.792 --> 15:02.227
- You can't fight that.
- I'll find a way,

15:02.328 --> 15:05.662
with the help of my snarky cat lawyer,
Meowsy McDermott.

15:05.766 --> 15:07.359
You've gotta be kitten me!

15:07.469 --> 15:08.800
Ha!

15:14.745 --> 15:15.906
This court finds

15:16.014 --> 15:18.779
in favor of the defendant,
McBurgertown Industries.

15:18.884 --> 15:21.115
